names are compared case-insensitively.\nKeep in mind that when importing shapefiles, property names may be\nmodified for backwards compatibility reasons. The names given by\n",[62,84,88],{"className":85,"displayText":86,"permalink":87},[69],"gis:property-names","gis",[22,89,86],{"className":90,"dataDisplayText":86,"href":91,"rel":92,"target":78,"title":86},[74],"/gis#property-names",[77]," can always be trusted as authoritative. For\nmanually specifying a mapping between property names and variable\nnames, see the ",[62,95,98],{"className":96,"displayText":97,"permalink":87},[69],"gis:create-turtles-inside-polygon-manual",[22,99,97],{"className":100,"dataDisplayText":97,"href":101,"rel":102,"target":78,"title":97},[74],"/gis#create-turtles-inside-polygon-manual",[77]," primitive.",[58,105,106],{},"Built-in variables such as “label” and “heading” are supported.\nNetLogo color numeric representations are supported for setting\n“color” and “label-color”, as well as the 15 default color string\nrepresentations (“red”, “blue”, “black”, etc.).",[58,108,109,110,119,120,128],{},"As an example: say you had a VectorDataset of polygons representing\ndifferent zip codes within a state and you want to create 100\ndifferent turtles within each zip code and have each turtle\nknow which zip code it originated in. The VectorDataset\nhas a field named “zip”, so you should add a variable\nnamed “zip” to the turtles with ",[62,111,114],{"className":112,"displayText":113,"permalink":113},[69],"turtles-own",[22,115,113],{"className":116,"dataDisplayText":113,"href":117,"rel":118,"target":78,"title":113},[74],"/dictionary#turtles-own",[77],". Then,\nloop through each VectorFeature in the VectorDataset and use\nthe ",[62,121,123],{"className":122,"displayText":25,"permalink":87},[69],[22,124,25],{"className":125,"dataDisplayText":25,"href":126,"rel":127,"target":78,"title":25},[74],"/gis#create-turtles-inside-polygon",[77]," primitive to create 100\nnew turtles.",[130,131,132],"pre",{},[62